<font class="content">Posted On 2002-02-28 11:26:33 by <a href="http://">Charoth</a></td></tr></table></td></tr></table><br>I think I'm slowly driving the guild insane each time I'm forced to play my chanter on raids, my plan is falling into place perfectly, but more on that later.<br /><br />Kind of a slow week, big raid wise, but Monday was a lot of fun in the Hole, a 1 team exp group went down and when your halfling cleric deems he has too much mana, get ready for crowd control. Having about 10 mobs in camp at anyone time is interesting, when they're all light blue hitting for nothing. (read to learn the fate of the gello)<BR><BR>However, when said cleric pulls about every rat in the zone plus that hard hitting ratman guard and then about 2 or 3 rock golems and sprinkling of elementals in one go, you pretty much know the outcome. In comes, the uber level 1 rogue of halfling doom, Palanwen to save the day with a quick CR. Gello has been trying his hardest to pull the "Train King" crown off of Effix's head I think.<br /><br />Tuesday, *snore* Exp days are always so boring, I'm sure someone had fun in Velks, or that stupid zone Umbral (blah).<br /><br />Wednesday it was back in ToV to learn more and more about the West Wing. There may be lots of spoiler sites for everything in EQ, but if you can't boil water, you ain't cooking soup (err, that makes sense, kind of). So with our little strike force of 2 to 3 groups, me playing the everhateful chanter of doom, we start pulling stuff and killing stuff, and when you don't have shaman/mage debuff power, things like to run. Oh, that was fun. ;)<br /><br />With me running around complaining at everything, yelling Gnome Supremecy at any point throughout the night, I'm hoping I annoyed enough of us to make sure that they'll force the other enchanters to log on and come to ToV, or else they'll face the Evil that is me in chanter form.<br /><br />Today, I'm sure its more ToV fun, cause when you're in ToV, its always fun, right? Armor farming is fun, right? *EXPLODE*</td></tr></table></td></tr></table><br>


